1
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:18,199
Brother Tian...

2
00:00:18,899 --> 00:00:19,960
I messed up today.

3
00:00:20,519 --> 00:00:21,820
Didn't show you a good time, Brother.

4
00:00:22,559 --> 00:00:23,379
Next time, I promise.

5
00:00:24,059 --> 00:00:24,940
Did I say you could leave?

6
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:35,619
I heard you're the Dance King of South City.

7
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:37,340
Great at breakdancing.

8
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:38,299
I've never seen it.

9
00:00:38,479 --> 00:00:39,179
Have you guys seen it?

10
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:39,880
Nope.

11
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,039
Dance king, huh?

12
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,420
Why don't you show everyone, then?

13
00:00:46,619 --> 00:00:47,539
Babe, wanna see?

14
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:48,579
I sure do!

15
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:49,780
Give us a dance!

16
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:52,700
Brother Tian...

17
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:57,380
I'll make it up to you properly later.

18
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,359
From now on, my place...

19
00:01:02,259 --> 00:01:02,939
...is open to you anytime.

20
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:04,680
Just... just like your own home.

21
00:01:04,879 --> 00:01:05,680
Make myself at home?

22
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:07,280
It's too filthy.

23
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:08,939
Sun Biao.

24
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:10,239
Dance.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:12,000
Right now.

26
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:16,620
Start dancing.

27
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:18,659
Need a hand?

28
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,500
Forgot how to move?

29
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,219
Sun Biao, you're not human!

30
00:01:31,379 --> 00:01:31,980
Scumbag!

31
00:01:37,319 --> 00:01:37,959
Animal!

32
00:01:38,959 --> 00:01:39,659
Bastard!

33
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:40,480
Scum!

34
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:55,819
Sun Biao.

35
00:01:56,799 --> 00:01:57,340
Now get lost.

36
00:01:57,819 --> 00:01:58,579
Hand over the turf.

37
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,019
You don't run this place anymore.

38
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,620
You're asking for it!

39
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:02,819
Just you wait!

40
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:03,879
Scram!

41
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:09,680
Brother Biao!

42
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:20,300
Sun Biao, Sun Biao, you're pathetic,

43
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,360
scheming in the dance hall,

44
00:02:25,539 --> 00:02:28,840
ran a badger game and tripped yourself up,

45
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:31,560
now hurry home and wipe some windows!

46
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:32,300
Thank you!

47
00:02:33,099 --> 00:02:34,460
Chen Daguang, Dance King of the East Suburbs!

48
00:02:35,099 --> 00:02:36,560
Nobody does it like you, Daguang!

49
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:37,960
Real talent!

50
00:02:39,439 --> 00:02:40,039
Hey, bro...

51
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,319
Now that we took over the joint,

52
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:43,379
what's the plan next?

53
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:46,580
Yeah, Zhuzi.

54
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:47,900
What's the plan?

55
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:50,539
What do you mean, what's the plan?

56
00:02:51,159 --> 00:02:52,840
What, you take it over and just walk away?

57
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:54,939
No...

58
00:02:55,039 --> 00:02:56,419
I didn't think about it.

59
00:02:56,479 --> 00:02:57,419
Seeing you over there,

60
00:02:57,699 --> 00:02:58,860
having such a great time...

61
00:02:59,099 --> 00:02:59,840
How about...

62
00:03:01,099 --> 00:03:01,620
you run it?

63
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:04,460
Go ahead, run it.

64
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,659
Why look at me? Do what you want.

65
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:15,900
All right.

66
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:17,379
If I gotta run it, I'll run it.

67
00:03:17,699 --> 00:03:18,159
Zhuzi,

68
00:03:18,939 --> 00:03:20,020
you're great at fighting,

69
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,819
but do you know how to run a business?

70
00:03:22,439 --> 00:03:24,840
Why wouldn't I? Who're you dissing?

71
00:03:26,139 --> 00:03:27,860
Have you ever heard of

72
00:03:28,139 --> 00:03:29,580
a market economy?

73
00:03:30,479 --> 00:03:31,599
Do you even know what

74
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:34,900
resource optimization and allocation mean?

75
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,340
What the hell is resource optimization?

76
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:39,960
Watch the news once in a while!

77
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,699
From now on, all that shady crap

78
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:43,620
has to stop.

79
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,800
Do clean business, make clean money.

80
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:46,659
Nice!

81
00:03:46,699 --> 00:03:47,979
The lady boss has real guts!

82
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,699
Whoever breaks the rules from now on

83
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,840
gets dealt with!

84
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:52,979
Solid!

85
00:03:54,659 --> 00:03:55,259
Um...

86
00:03:55,819 --> 00:03:58,280
Thanks for helping Xiur today.

87
00:03:59,319 --> 00:04:01,240
Gotta say, your moves today...

88
00:04:01,319 --> 00:04:03,539
You were so manly!

89
00:04:03,759 --> 00:04:04,680
I didn't expect

90
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,460
you'd be so badass yourself.

91
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,520
Sun Biao with his half-assed skills,

92
00:04:10,659 --> 00:04:11,580
still dared to pick a fight with me!

93
00:04:12,039 --> 00:04:13,180
Next time I lay eyes on him,

94
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,080
I'll lead with a knuckle sandwich!

95
00:04:15,159 --> 00:04:15,939
I'll wipe that smirk right off his face!

96
00:04:17,839 --> 00:04:18,399
But...

97
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,920
are you really gonna run that dance hall?

98
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,360
Can you handle it?

99
00:04:23,699 --> 00:04:25,120
How would I know how to run a dance hall?

100
00:04:25,259 --> 00:04:26,379
I was just bragging to them!

101
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,399
We fool around,

102
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:28,240
have some fun, and call it a day!

103
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:29,819
That won't do!

104
00:04:29,959 --> 00:04:31,579
You gave your word.

105
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:33,019
You have to take responsibility!

106
00:04:34,439 --> 00:04:35,519
Well... all right.

107
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,339
I'll listen to you.

108
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:37,199
Then I'll go every day!

109
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:40,060
You can't go every day either!

110
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:41,600
You're a factory worker!

111
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:44,000
You made junior worker in just two years!

112
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,019
You gotta get back to the factory and work!

113
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,220
What do you want me to do, then?

114
00:04:49,939 --> 00:04:50,540
Relax.

115
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,339
I'll definitely be a good worker.

116
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,519
But that Ma Limin, I swear...

117
00:04:59,079 --> 00:05:00,519
Always harping on every petty thing,

118
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:02,019
dumping crap on my head,

119
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,899
making me write endless self-criticisms!

120
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,399
What kind of demon beast is he anyway?

121
00:05:08,439 --> 00:05:09,079
Just you wait.

122
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,300
If he acts cocky around me again,

123
00:05:10,439 --> 00:05:11,480
bossing me around like that,

124
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:12,540
I'll lead right off and...

125
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:13,980
I'll serve him two knuckle sandwiches!

126
00:05:20,399 --> 00:05:20,879
Officer,

127
00:05:21,379 --> 00:05:22,639
I've told you everything.

128
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,360
That's pretty much what happened.

129
00:05:26,199 --> 00:05:28,779
Liu Haizhu was truly doing a good deed,

130
00:05:29,199 --> 00:05:30,160
helping out a coworker.

131
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,959
We just hope you can help

132
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:34,620
by issuing an official statement

133
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:36,639
straight to our factory, okay?

134
00:05:36,879 --> 00:05:37,800
Look, here's the thing.

135
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:38,720
As for his case,

136
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:39,860
we closed it long ago.

137
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:41,259
If you need it,

138
00:05:41,399 --> 00:05:42,540
we can issue you

139
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:44,319
a certificate of no criminal record. Okay?

140
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:45,939
I already told you,

141
00:05:46,019 --> 00:05:47,319
that's of no use!

142
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:50,019
You need to prove he did something good.

143
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,759
This happened because you went to the factory

144
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,839
and hauled him off in front of everyone!

145
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:56,740
Now people have the wrong idea,

146
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,500
and everyone's gossiping about him!

147
00:05:58,819 --> 00:05:59,420
Look, friend,

148
00:05:59,579 --> 00:06:01,199
you really can't blame us.

149
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,160
We were just summoning him by law.

150
00:06:03,639 --> 00:06:05,139
But the way you handled the case

151
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:07,160
caused such a bad fallout for him.

152
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,680
You need to clean up the mess!

153
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:10,860
Come on, now.

154
00:06:11,259 --> 00:06:12,500
I've been chatting with you this whole time.

155
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:13,480
If you've got time for this,

156
00:06:13,579 --> 00:06:14,660
go back and talk to Liu Haizhu.

157
00:06:14,779 --> 00:06:15,899
Tell him to stop causing trouble.

158
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:16,459
He—

159
00:06:19,439 --> 00:06:20,560
Officials who don't care about the people...

160
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,339
What's with that guy talking like that?

161
00:06:25,779 --> 00:06:26,980
I was being perfectly polite!

162
00:06:50,699 --> 00:06:51,199
What're you doing?

163
00:06:52,899 --> 00:06:53,279
Uncle!

164
00:06:53,699 --> 00:06:54,180
You're back.

165
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:54,899
Just working.

166
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:57,879
Rough trip, huh?

167
00:06:58,639 --> 00:06:59,079
Here.

168
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,600
Just brewed some tea for you.

169
00:07:02,439 --> 00:07:02,899
So, how is it?

170
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:04,500
While I was away from the factory...

171
00:07:04,819 --> 00:07:05,579
did anyone stir up trouble?

172
00:07:05,879 --> 00:07:06,500
Who'd dare?

173
00:07:07,180 --> 00:07:08,480
Under your wise leadership,

174
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:09,579
we're thriving here.

175
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,720
United, driven, and full of ambition!

176
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:11,620
All right, all right, enough.

177
00:07:12,519 --> 00:07:13,759
I'm sick of your flattery.

178
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,339
What about Zhou Meng and Liu Haizhu?

179
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:17,819
Bring me his self-criticism letter.

180
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:18,360
Let me see it.

181
00:07:21,319 --> 00:07:22,160
Wait, Uncle...

182
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:24,300
Forget the self-criticism for now.

183
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,199
I heard Liu Haizhu and Zhou Meng...

184
00:07:27,959 --> 00:07:29,639
started a little side business outside.

185
00:07:30,439 --> 00:07:31,819
They're living the good life.

186
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:38,180
Doing pretty well for themselves.

187
00:07:42,139 --> 00:07:42,579
Boss!

188
00:07:43,579 --> 00:07:44,779
Look at 'em, all beat to hell!

189
00:07:44,879 --> 00:07:45,959
What happened, Boss?

190
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:47,259
Brother Li brought us to run the turf...

191
00:07:47,519 --> 00:07:47,920
Get inside!

192
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,420
Beat to a pulp and you still wanna run the turf?

193
00:07:54,459 --> 00:07:55,399
Where'd you go, Boss?

194
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:56,839
The big cases aren't solved yet...

195
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,319
but we can't let the small ones slide either.

196
00:07:58,779 --> 00:07:59,079
Right?

197
00:07:59,120 --> 00:07:59,720
Officer Kong.

198
00:08:00,259 --> 00:08:00,920
Sign here, please.

199
00:08:00,939 --> 00:08:01,339
Sure thing.

200
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:04,439
Here, give it to me.

201
00:08:06,339 --> 00:08:07,000
Well, you see...

202
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:08,259
someone at the shipyard tipped us off.

203
00:08:08,819 --> 00:08:10,339
A theft ring from the West Suburbs...

204
00:08:10,939 --> 00:08:11,480
Busted the whole lot of 'em.

205
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:12,879
Great. Thanks!

206
00:08:13,579 --> 00:08:15,279
A shipyard worker?

207
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:15,740
Yep.

208
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,000
Boss...

209
00:08:18,379 --> 00:08:19,459
The guy who gave the tip...

210
00:08:19,899 --> 00:08:21,579
he wouldn't happen to be Liu Haizhu, would he?

211
00:08:22,079 --> 00:08:22,879
I did nothing wrong!

212
00:08:23,439 --> 00:08:24,180
They had it coming!

213
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:25,180
They're thugs!

214
00:08:25,279 --> 00:08:26,220
They're thieves!

215
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:28,959
They're thugs and thieves!

216
00:08:29,459 --> 00:08:30,220
Do you have proof?

217
00:08:30,339 --> 00:08:31,139
Did you catch 'em red-handed?

218
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,340
Is there a police report?

219
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,240
Of course I filed a report!

220
00:08:34,519 --> 00:08:35,659
When my bike was stolen back then...

221
00:08:35,759 --> 00:08:36,720
they're the ones who stole it!

222
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:38,600
I even had to go to Lijiatun to get it back myself!

223
00:08:38,659 --> 00:08:40,220
That's a separate matter.

224
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:42,539
We're talking about your river assault.

225
00:08:44,139 --> 00:08:45,139
It really is Liu Haizhu!

226
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,100
This guy deserves some praise.

227
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:48,240
Old Kong!

228
00:08:48,379 --> 00:08:48,879
Coming!

229
00:08:50,139 --> 00:08:52,360
You've gotta prove he did a good deed!

230
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:55,019
It's just because you went to the factory...

231
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,200
and took him away in front of everyone!

232
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,120
Now a lot of folks got the wrong idea...

233
00:08:59,279 --> 00:09:00,879
and started gossiping about him.

234
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:10,360
Feng Ziwen, what're you afraid of?

235
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:11,899
Pedal faster!

236
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,720
Hurry up.

237
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:27,340
Be careful.

238
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,080
How did you find this place?

239
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,019
Right after I got out,

240
00:09:43,379 --> 00:09:45,019
I had nowhere to go,

241
00:09:45,379 --> 00:09:46,500
so I rode my bike here.

242
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,000
Sat by the river,

243
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:49,039
looked up,

244
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:50,480
and thought it was a nice spot.

245
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:52,460
What are you looking at?

246
00:09:53,139 --> 00:09:53,759
Just seeing

247
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,559
if I can see farther out.

248
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:04,539
I used to think

249
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:06,799
Songliao was pretty big,

250
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,360
but turns out it's only this small.

251
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,139
There are so many places I don't recognize.

252
00:10:11,779 --> 00:10:12,940
Songliao's always been this size.

253
00:10:13,879 --> 00:10:15,200
You've just gotten bolder.

254
00:10:15,399 --> 00:10:16,820
There you go teasing me again.

255
00:10:18,059 --> 00:10:19,320
I remember it so clearly.

256
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:20,879
Over there was the edge of town,

257
00:10:21,019 --> 00:10:22,960
and past that were the outskirts.

258
00:10:24,379 --> 00:10:25,220
When you were a kid,

259
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,259
you always thought

260
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,159
leaving the alley meant leaving town.

261
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,879
Stop teasing me!

262
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,360
Brother Ziwen,

263
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:44,860
you care so much about Brother Zhuzi.

264
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:46,820
Is it because he can fight,

265
00:10:47,139 --> 00:10:47,960
or is it

266
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:50,419
because of what happened back then?

267
00:10:55,559 --> 00:10:56,919
Plenty of guys can fight in this world,

268
00:10:57,399 --> 00:10:58,360
and plenty aren't afraid to die.

269
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,659
Zhuzi's a bit naive.

270
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:03,639
He's stubborn,

271
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:04,779
and believes in justice.

272
00:11:06,139 --> 00:11:06,779
Deep inside,

273
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:08,179
there's a place

274
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,860
that filth can never touch.

275
00:11:13,879 --> 00:11:16,519
Sounds a bit like the old you.

276
00:11:21,779 --> 00:11:22,580
If...

277
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:24,259
I mean, what if...

278
00:11:26,139 --> 00:11:27,740
that thing hadn't happened back then,

279
00:11:28,639 --> 00:11:29,720
would you

280
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,340
have chosen differently?

281
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:34,559
There are no what-ifs.

282
00:11:43,059 --> 00:11:44,360
But in my heart,

283
00:11:45,899 --> 00:11:47,539
you'll always be the same Feng Ziwen.

284
00:11:49,299 --> 00:11:50,139
Always.

285
00:12:15,299 --> 00:12:15,960
Hey...

286
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:18,679
Let me give you something.

287
00:12:27,399 --> 00:12:28,080
Careful with it.

288
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:29,000
This...

289
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:32,480
This little thing looks like a toy.

290
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,220
Can't even chop vegetables with it.

291
00:12:35,159 --> 00:12:35,700
Then I'll take it back.

292
00:12:35,779 --> 00:12:36,279
No way.

293
00:12:36,519 --> 00:12:37,860
You already promised to give it to me.

294
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:48,000
When spring comes and the ice melts...

295
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:50,080
where does the river flow to?

296
00:12:51,159 --> 00:12:52,600
Probably pretty far.

297
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,240
Down the river into the sea.

298
00:12:56,919 --> 00:12:57,779
The sea?

299
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,159
What's the sea like?

300
00:13:01,639 --> 00:13:02,500
I've never seen it either.

301
00:13:03,659 --> 00:13:04,659
But we've gotta see it someday.

302
00:13:07,279 --> 00:13:09,379
Then when spring comes...

303
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,240
take me to see it, will you?

304
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,240
It's a deal.

305
00:13:27,559 --> 00:13:28,019
Zhou Meng,

306
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:31,240
you've got a letter.

307
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:39,659
Thanks.

308
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,159
Attention, all factory staff.

309
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:44,279
Maintenance worker Liu Haizhu

310
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:48,159
has repeatedly gathered with street thugs

311
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:50,820
and engaged in severe brawls.

312
00:13:51,139 --> 00:13:52,639
The circumstances are extremely serious,

313
00:13:52,779 --> 00:13:54,340
and the impact is highly detrimental.

314
00:13:54,779 --> 00:13:55,840
After due consideration,

315
00:13:56,159 --> 00:13:57,820
it is decided to issue worker Liu Haizhu

316
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,539
a serious demerit.

317
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:02,460
You're still working a bit too slow.

318
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:03,500
This won't do.

319
00:14:04,139 --> 00:14:05,700
It may be getting colder,

320
00:14:05,919 --> 00:14:07,259
but your enthusiasm has got to go up.

321
00:14:07,519 --> 00:14:07,980
Right?

322
00:14:08,419 --> 00:14:09,440
You've gotta put some muscle into it.

323
00:14:10,779 --> 00:14:11,460
Make it snappy.

324
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,460
Apologize right now and talk properly!

325
00:14:14,519 --> 00:14:15,000
Did you hear me?

326
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:15,840
Fix your attitude.

327
00:14:16,159 --> 00:14:16,980
This is way too sloppy.

328
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:17,899
Director Ma!

329
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,019
Sharp eyes as always!

330
00:14:20,259 --> 00:14:20,740
Director Ma.

331
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:23,320
Look, about this matter,

332
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,519
you must have misunderstood.

333
00:14:25,679 --> 00:14:26,580
The boy doesn't know any better.

334
00:14:27,179 --> 00:14:28,759
He's caused you and the plant big trouble.

335
00:14:29,259 --> 00:14:30,059
Today, I'm...

336
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:31,360
swallowing my pride

337
00:14:31,679 --> 00:14:32,399
to beg you for leniency.

338
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,919
Could you let him off the hook?

339
00:14:35,779 --> 00:14:36,559
Here, take this.

340
00:14:36,779 --> 00:14:37,220
Old Liu.

341
00:14:37,419 --> 00:14:38,000
Old Liu.

342
00:14:39,519 --> 00:14:41,059
You're a veteran worker here.

343
00:14:42,059 --> 00:14:43,000
You know how the rules work.

344
00:14:43,879 --> 00:14:45,940
What your son did is no small offense.

345
00:14:46,779 --> 00:14:47,860
You want me to let it slide?

346
00:14:48,039 --> 00:14:49,159
What about the factory's regulations?

347
00:14:49,279 --> 00:14:50,019
Am I supposed to just toss them out?

348
00:14:51,299 --> 00:14:52,299
Besides,

349
00:14:52,879 --> 00:14:54,899
it's not like we didn't give him a chance.

350
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:56,559
We told him to write a self-criticism, but he refused.

351
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:57,799
Look at him.

352
00:14:58,460 --> 00:14:59,139
Even right now,

353
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,200
he's still acting like this.

354
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:01,639
With an attitude like that,

355
00:15:01,779 --> 00:15:02,919
what else do you expect me to say?

356
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,259
Dad, why even waste your breath on him?

357
00:15:05,379 --> 00:15:06,620
Like a broken bike, asking for a kicking!

358
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:07,779
What's the point of talking to him?

359
00:15:08,539 --> 00:15:09,539
You're the one asking for a kicking!

360
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:10,659
Wait.

361
00:15:11,139 --> 00:15:11,860
Did I hear that right?

362
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:12,659
You heard him right.

363
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:13,700
No, he didn't mean you!

364
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:15,679
Liu Haizhu...

365
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:17,299
Aren't you something?

366
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,259
In front of your father today,

367
00:15:20,779 --> 00:15:22,139
I'll tell you one more time.

368
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:23,340
What about it?

369
00:15:24,379 --> 00:15:25,919
Due to your repeated misconduct

370
00:15:26,159 --> 00:15:26,960
and refusal to reform,

371
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:28,440
the factory has officially decided

372
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:31,399
to issue you a serious demerit.

373
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:34,139
All relevant benefits and bonuses

374
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,200
are completely revoked!

375
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,799
No, Director Ma, Director Ma!

376
00:15:39,179 --> 00:15:39,700
Director Ma!

377
00:15:40,139 --> 00:15:40,539
Director Ma!

378
00:15:41,679 --> 00:15:42,220
Director Ma!

379
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:43,360
Look...

380
00:15:44,019 --> 00:15:44,940
The boy is young,

381
00:15:45,419 --> 00:15:46,240
and it's his first offense.

382
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:48,879
A demerit is out of the question!

383
00:15:49,559 --> 00:15:50,519
If you put that on his record,

384
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,299
his whole life will be ruined!

385
00:15:52,399 --> 00:15:52,960
Don't you think?

386
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:54,279
Here, please.

387
00:15:54,799 --> 00:15:56,519
Have a smoke and cool off.

388
00:15:56,659 --> 00:15:57,740
No smoking in the workshop!

389
00:15:57,820 --> 00:15:58,740
Just calm down, all right?

390
00:15:58,879 --> 00:15:59,700
Cut that crap out!

391
00:16:05,659 --> 00:16:06,580
What are you doing, Ma Limin?

392
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:07,659
Pick it up!

393
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:09,700
What? What of it?

394
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:10,779
You gonna hit me?

395
00:16:11,259 --> 00:16:12,580
I said pick it up. Did you hear me?

396
00:16:12,679 --> 00:16:13,139
Get back here.

397
00:16:13,899 --> 00:16:14,379
What?

398
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:15,860
Squat down.

399
00:16:17,379 --> 00:16:17,820
Pick it up.

400
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:19,600
Look at you, acting so tough.

401
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:21,659
The grown-ups got no decency,

402
00:16:21,759 --> 00:16:22,720
and the kids got no manners.

403
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:23,320
Right?

404
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:24,580
Got no mother at home,

405
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:26,360
so no one taught you how to act, huh?

406
00:16:29,379 --> 00:16:31,059
Ma Limin, fuck your ancestors!

407
00:16:32,179 --> 00:16:32,639
What are you doing?!

408
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:33,440
I'll fucking kill you!

409
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:34,960
You bullied my son!

410
00:16:36,019 --> 00:16:37,080
You bullied my son!
